</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Information - Rights Issue in Independent Oil & Resources PLC<br><br>There will be carried out a Rights Issue in Independent Oil & Resources PLC ("the Company"). The background for this is that the Board wishes to further develop the Company by strengthening its capital base for investment opportunities and to follow up on the Company's existing investment positions and its commitments through its daughters. The Rights Issue comprises an offering of up to 200 000 000 New Shares, with a subscription price of NOK 0.07 per share. The Board has decided not to engage any broker house for the Rights Issue, but will carry out the Rights Issue itself. <br><br>The invitation for this Rights Issue is sent to the 149 biggest shareholders in the company as of 8. August 2014. The Subscription Period in the Offering will last from and including 11 August 2014 to and including 25 August 2014. The book will close at 17:30 hours (Cyprus time) on 25 August 2014 after which no further orders will be accepted. <br><br>All shareholders who have received this invitation are invited to actively consider whether they would like to subscribe for New Shares. <br><br>Allocation of New Shares will be based on the number of shares subscribed.  In case of over-subscription, allocation will be determined based on a pro rata basis based on the number of shares held by the shareholder prior to the Offering.<br><br>No Prospectus has been prepared for this Offering as the number of invited investors do not exceed 150.  Enclosed please find unaudited financial statements for the period Jan-Jun 2014.<br><br>For Subscription, please notify the Company within the closing date either by fax +357 25 356 500 or by email to ddemou@fidelius.com.cy<br><br><br><br><br>Sincerely <br>Independent Oil & Resources PLC<br>Jan Egil Moe, Chairman<br><br><br>Limassol 12/08/2014</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
<a href="/public/news/14651.pdf">
FS 30 06 2014- (Unaudited).pdf</a>
</td>
</tr>
