<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>IO&R has on 08 June 2009 completed a private placement of a total of 45,000,000 new shares, an increase of 11.8%, at a subscription price of NOK 0.20 per share. The gross proceeds from the private placement amounts to NOK 9,000,000.<br><br>The proceeds from the private placement will be used to strengthen IO&R's cash position hereunder reduce its debt related to investments. <br><br>Upon registration of the new shares issued in the private placement, IO&R's share capital will amount to NOK 10,650,153.65 - corresponding to 426,006,146 shares, each with a par value of NOK 0.025.<br><br>Following the transaction the company's two main shareholders, Increased Oil Recovery AS and Independent Oilfield Rentals Ltd. (including it's wholly owned company NET AS) own 139.590.925 shares (32.8%) and 126.895.502 shares, respectively. <br><br> <br>Independent Oil and Resources ASA<br>Board of Directors, 09 June  2009</p></td>
