</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>1.	Summons to ordinary general meeting<br><br>In a board meeting on 12 May 2006, IOTA resolved to call an ordinary general meeting on 22 June 2006. The precise time and place of the general meeting will appear from the summons, which will be sent out in week 19.<br><br><br>2.	Proposal of new legal structure<br><br>The board of IOTA has further resolved to put a proposal before the general meeting on 22 June, to reorganize the legal structure of the company. The reorganization will entail the establishment of a holding model, after which IOTA’s operational activities will be placed in a wholly-owned subsidiary company, IOT Services AS. The administrative functions and the financial investments will remain in IOTA.<br><br>The reorganization will be carried out by demerging the operational activities of IOTA into a newly founded company, IOT Reorg AS, and in exchange, the shareholders of IOTA will be given shares in IOT Reorg AS. IOT Reorg AS will then be immediately merged with IOT Services, and in exchange, the shareholders of IOT Reorg AS will be given shares in IOTA.<br><br>After the completion of the reorganization, IOTA’s shareholders will have the same number of shares in IOTA, with the same nominal value, as prior to the reorganization. The reorganization will not bring about any tax related effects for Norwegian companies or Norwegian shareholders. Foreign shareholders must seek the necessary professional assistance to assess any tax related effects of the reorganization. <br><br>In practice, the mentioned demerger and merger will come into effect at the same time, and the aim is that the completion will take place in August or September 2006. The transaction will be carried out during a week-end after the end of trading on a Friday and be completed before the trade opens Monday morning. Thus, the shares in IOTA can be traded as usual during the whole period.<br><br>The background for the board’s proposal is to create a clear division of operational and organisational tasks and responsibilities, with an increased focus on operations. A further aim is to entail cost savings for the corporation and make the underlying values in IOTA more visible.<br><br>For further information, please contact:<br><br>Erik Solheim, Chairman of the Board of Independent Oil Tools ASA, tel +47 55 56 82 00<br><br><br>Bergen/Stavanger 12 May 2006.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://www.independent.no">
http://www.independent.no</a>
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>IOTA - INNKALLING TIL ORDINÆR GENERALFORSAMLING OG FORSLAG OM NY JURIDISK STRUKTUR</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-05-12 15:45:34</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>1.	Innkalling til ordinær generalforsamling<br><br>IOTA har i styremøte den 12. mai 2006 besluttet å innkalle til ordinær generalforsamling den 22. juni 2006. Nøyaktig tid og sted for generalforsamlingen vil fremkomme av innkallingen som vil bli sendt ut i løpet av uke 19.<br><br>2.	Forslag om ny juridisk struktur<br><br>Styret i IOTA har videre besluttet å forslå overfor generalforsamlingen den 22. juni 2006 å reorganisere selskapets juridiske struktur. Reorganiseringen innebærer at det etableres en såkalt holding¬modell, hvoretter IOTAs operasjonelle virksomhet vil bli liggende i et heleiet datterselskap, IOT Services AS. Administrative funksjoner og finansielle investeringer vil bli liggende i IOTA.<br><br>Reorganiseringen gjennomføres ved at den operasjonelle virksomheten i IOTA utfisjoneres til et nyetablert selskap, IOT Reorg AS mot at aksjonærene i IOTA får aksjer i IOT Reorg AS. IOT Reorg AS fusjoneres deretter umiddelbart med IOT Services mot at aksjonærene i IOT Reorg AS får aksjer i IOTA.<br><br>Etter at reorganiseringen er gjennomført vil aksjonærene i IOTA ha samme antall aksjer i IOTA med samme pålydende som forut for reorganiseringen. Reorganiseringen utløser ingen skattemessige effekter for norske selskaper eller norske aksjonærer.  Utenlandske aksjonærer må selv søke nødvendig bistand for å vurdere eventuelle skattemessige effekter av reorganiseringen. <br><br>Praktisk vil nevnte fisjon og fusjon tre i kraft samtidig, og det tas sikte på at dette vil skje i løpet av august eller september 2006. Transaksjonen skal gjennomføres over en weekend mellom handleslutt fredag og før handelen åpner på mandag morgen. Aksjene i IOTA kan således omsettes som normalt under hele perioden.<br><br>Bakgrunnen for styrets forslag er å skape en oversiktlig og klar arbeids- og ansvarsfordeling med økt fokus på drift.  Reorganiseringen antas også å medføre besparelser for konsernet og at verdier i IOTA blir bedre synliggjort.<br><br>Ytterligere opplysninger kan fås ved henvendelser til:<br><br>Erik Solheim, styreformann i Independent Oil Tools ASA, tel +47 55 56 82 00<br><br><br>Bergen/Stavanger 12. mai 2006.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://www.independent.no">
http://www.independent.no</a>
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>IOT ASA – Information regarding shareholding in Petrojack ASA.</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2006-05-05 08:31:21</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Reference is made to the stock exchange announcement from Petrojack ASA on april 4th 2006 regarding<br>a conditional agreement to sell the ownership of Petrojack’s three jackup rigs for an aggregate price of approximately USD 600 mill. The announcement states that a.o the agreement is conditional on approval by the general assembly of Petrojack ASA.<br><br>The board of Directors of  IOT ASA have in a board meeting decided not to vote in favour of a sale of all three rigs as described in the above mentioned announcement, when and if  the general assembly is invited to approve the sale.<br><br><br>IOT ASA holds 20 880 069 shares in Petrojack ASA (including options and forward contracts) equal to 34,41 % of the shares outstanding</p></td>
</tr>
