<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2005-12-13 10:33:54</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Independent Oil Tools ASA (”IOT”) has on December 12. 2005 sold 26,122,441 shares in Petrolia Drilling ASA at NOK 2.60 per share. After the above mentioned acquisition, IOT holds 120,015,686 shares in Petrolia Drilling, equal to 27,1% of the shares outstanding.<br><br>IOT holds an additional 11,716,673 subscription rights (each giving IOT right to subscribe one new share in Petrolia Drilling ASA at NOK 0.55 per share), and a convertible bond loan with a nominal value of NOK 4,500,000, with an exercise <br>price of NOK 0.47 per share (as the exercise price cannot be lower than the nominal value per share in Petrolia Drilling ASA of NOK 0.50 per share, an exercise price of NOK 0.50 is assumed, with IOT being compensated for the difference in cash), convertible into 9.000.000 new shares in Petrolia Drilling ASA.<br><br>In total, IOT holds shares and rights corresponding to a total of 140,732,359 shares in Petrolia Drilling ASA, corresponding to 29,0% of the fully diluted shares (485,459,202) in Petrolia Drilling ASA<br><br><br>Stavanger, December 13, 2005</p></td>
</tr>
