<td><h2>IOT ASA - PRIVATE PLACEMENT COMPLETED</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2005-12-02 09:16:51</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Reference is made to the OTC-announcement by Independent Oil Tools ASA (“IOT”) on December 1, 2005. <br><br>On December 1, 2005 IOT completed a private placement of 23,000,000 new shares, at a subscription price of NOK 2.20 per share. Total gross proceeds from the private placement equals NOK 50,600,000. <br><br><br>After registration of the private placement, the share capital of IOT will increase from NOK 5,250,153,65 to NOK 5,825,153.65, and the number of shares, each with a nominal value of NOK 0.025, will increase from 210,006,146 to 233,006,146.<br><br>The proceeds from the private placement will be used to finance further investments in accordance with IOT’s strategy, and repayment of leasing debt on the equipment recently transferred to Petrolia Drilling ASA.<br><br><br>Independent Oil Tools ASA, <br><br><br>Stavanger, December 2, 2005</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://www.independent.no">
http://www.independent.no</a>
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>IOT ASA - Considers private placement</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2005-12-01 16:06:25</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Independent Oil Tools ASA (“IOT”) intends to carry out a private placement with gross proceeds of approximately MNOK 50. The private placement will be marketed to professional investors in the period from 16:10 to 18:00 (Norwegian time) on Thursday December 1, 2005. The subscription price shall be close to market price on Thursday December 1, 2005.<br><br>The planned private placement shall be carried out based on the existing board authorization given by the general meeting on October 17, 2005.<br><br>The proceeds from the planned private placement shall be used to finance further investments in accordance with IOT’s strategy, and repay leasing debt on equipment recently sold to Petrolia Drilling ASA.<br><br><br>Independent Oil Tools ASA, Board or Directors<br><br>Stavanger, December 1, 2005</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://www.independent.no">
http://www.independent.no</a>
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>IOT ASA - Petrolia Drilling ASA -  Disclosure of shareholdings</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2005-11-29 10:01:47</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Petrolia Drilling ASA – flagging (disclosure of large shareholdings and rights to shares)<br><br>Reference is made to Petrolia Drilling ASA’s stock exchange announcement dated November 29, 2005 regarding purchase of drilling equipment and share capital increase.<br><br>Independent Oil Tools ASA (”IOT”) has subscribed 93,777,030 new shares, at NOK 0.55 per share, in a private placement in Petrolia Drilling ASA, and has exercised 23,389,697 subscription rights, each right giving IOT one new share in Petrolia Drilling ASA at a subscription price of NOK 0.55 per share. <br><br>After the private placement and the exercise of subscription rights, IOT holds 146,138,127 shares in Petrolia Drilling ASA, corresponding to 32.97% of the new number of shares in Petrolia Drilling ASA. <br><br>IOT holds an additional 11,716,673 subscription rights (each giving IOT right to subscribe one new share in Petrolia Drilling ASA at NOK 0.55 per share), and a convertible bond loan with a nominal value of NOK 4,500,000, with an exercise price of NOK 0.47 per share (as the exercise price cannot be lower than the nominal value per share in Petrolia Drilling ASA of NOK 0.50 per share, an exercise price of NOK 0.50 is assumed, with IOT being compensated for the difference in cash), convertible into 9.000.000 new shares in Petrolia Drilling ASA.<br><br>In total, IOT will after the private placement and exercise of the subscription rights own shares and rights to a total of 166,854,800 shares in Petrolia Drilling ASA, corresponding to 37.64% of the new number of outstanding shares in Petrolia Drilling ASA after the private placement and the exercise of the subscription rights, and 34.37% of the fully diluted number of shares (485,459,202) in Petrolia Drilling ASA.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://www.independent.no">
http://www.independent.no</a>
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>IOT ASA  -  Preliminary financial report, 3rd quarter 2005</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2005-11-07 12:46:41</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Please find enclosed financial report for Independent Oil Tools ASA, (IOT) including Premium Casing Services Pty. Ltd., (PCS) for Q3 2005. <br><br>Total revenue for Q3 is mill NOK 30,6 and operating expenses are mill NOK 25,6. PCS accounts for mill NOK 10,7 of the revenue and mill NOK 10,1 of the operating expenses.<br><br>Operating result is mill NOK 4,99 and income before tax is mill NOK 4,85, down from mill NOK 7,7 in Q2. However, and as previously reported, Q2 pretax result included sale of surplus equipment, amounting to mill NOK 3,6.   <br><br>While PCS`s activity was somewhat behind budget in Q3, mainly due to delayed start-up of contracts, IOT`s core rental activity in the North Sea area was very good for the 3rd quarter and well above budget.  <br><br>Activity is expected to remain high also for the 4th quarter for IOT`s core areas, and some improvement is expected also for PCS` activities, as delayed operations are getting started.  <br><br>IOT will continue to look for investment opportunities, particularly in the rig market, which remains very strong.   <br><br><br><br>Independent Oil Tools ASA<br>7th November 2005<br><br>Contact person:<br><br>Harald Smedsvik<br>General manager<br>Tel.: (+47) 51 81 94 00</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://www.independent.no">
http://www.independent.no</a>
<a href="/public/news/3591.doc">
Kvartalsregnskap 3. Q-2005.doc</a>
</td>
</tr>
