<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>IOT ASA - Preliminary financial report, 2nd Quarter 2005</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2005-07-21 14:39:50</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Please find below financial report for Independent Oil Tools ASA for Q2 2005. (all amounts in NOK thousands)<br><br>Total revenue is 21.782, up from 17.694 in Q1, while operating result is 6.553, up from 2.618 in Q1.  <br><br>Net income before tax is 7.714, after extra-ordinary income of 1.019 and net financial income of 142; up from 1.077 in Q1. <br><br>Revenue for the core business is 21.341, operating result is 6.724 and net income before tax is 7.628, incl. extraordinary income of 1.019, which is 3.940 above budget. Net income includes  sale of surplus equipment. <br><br>After a busy Q1, activity has slowed down somewhat. While the Norwegian Petroleum Directorate (NPD) predicted at the beginning of the year that 30 – 35 exploration- and appraisal wells would be drilled in 2005, only 6 wells were drilled as per 30.06, basically due to a shortage of rigs available to drill the planned wells. <br>This obviously has a negative impact on our core business in the short term. However, the planned wells will be drilled in due time.      <br><br><br>Independent Oil Tools ASA<br>20th July 2005<br><br>Contact person:<br><br>Harald Smedsvik<br>General manager<br>Tel. (+47) 51 81 94 10</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://www.independent.no">
http://www.independent.no</a>
<a href="/public/news/3193.doc">
Kvartalsregnskap 2. Q-2005.doc</a>
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>IOT ASA - Avtale om overdragelse  av aksjer i PDR ASA</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2005-07-04 09:59:56</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Independent Oil Tools ASA (”IOT”) har den 1. juli 2005 inngått avtale om overdragelse av 21.428.600 aksjer i Petrolia Drilling ASA (”Petrolia Drilling”).<br><br>IOT vil etter at overdragelsen har funnet sted eie 28.971.400 aksjer i Petrolia Drilling, tilsvarende 8,9 % av antall utestående aksjer i Petrolia Drilling.<br><br>IOT eier også rettigheter til aksjer i Petrolia Drilling i form av (i) konvertible obligasjoner pålydende NOK 4.500.000, med konverteringskurs NOK 0,47 per aksje, som kan konverteres til 9.574.468 aksjer i Petrolia Drilling i perioden frem til februar 2006, og (ii) 128.883.400 frittstående tegningsretter som hver gir rett til tegning av 1 ny aksje i Petrolia Drilling, til kurs NOK 0,55 per aksje, i perioden frem til mars 2006.  <br><br>IOT vil etter at overdragelsen av de 21.428.600 aksjene i Petrolia Drilling har funnet sted eie aksjer og rettigheter til totalt 167.429.268 aksjer i Petrolia Drilling, tilsvarende 51,5% av antall utestående aksjer (325.417.347) i Petrolia Drilling og 34,4% av fullt utvannet antall aksjer (486.271.003) i Petrolia Drilling.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://www.independent.no">
http://www.independent.no</a>
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>IOT ASA  acquires Premium Casing Services Pty. Ltd.</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2005-06-28 12:58:22</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Independent Oil Tools ASA (“IOT”) has entered into an agreement to acquire all outstanding shares of Premium Casing Services Pty. Ltd. (“Premium”).<br><br>Premium is a leading Australian provider of tubular running services, casing, completions / preassembly makeup, wireline equipment rental and personnel. Premium is also the sole test rig provider in the Southern Hemisphere. Premium has approximately 72 employees in Western (Perth) and Central (Adelaide) Australia, serving Australia and surrounding regions. Premium is in the process of establishing an office and warehouse facility in New Zealand. Furthermore, Premium has been added to the Petronas tender list for upcoming submissions in September 2005, and upon award of any contract, Premium will establish facilities in Malaysia. <br><br>IOT shall pay a total compensation of (i) NOK 20 000 000 in cash, (ii) 21 428 571 shares in Petrolia Drilling ASA (“PDR), and (iii) 28 145 162 shares in IOT (based on the authorization given by the general meeting in IOT on May 24, 2005) to the owners (Independent Oilfield Rentals IOR Ltd. (45.8%), Bernh. Larsen Holding AS (45.8%) and Premium’s managing director (8.4%)) of Premium. <br><br>As per June 27, 2005, the value of the purchase price equals approximately NOK 88.5 million (based on a price per PDR-share of NOK 0.70 and a price per IOT-share of NOK 1.90). <br><br>The Board of Directors of IOT is pleased to announce its first important acquisition, expanding IOT’s international presence. The acquisition of Premium is expected to strengthen IOT’s rental and equipment operations. Based on its position in tubular and casing services, Premium intends to increase its focus on the rental segment in the Southern Hemisphere, using IOT’s rental experience. <br><br>IOT is considering other international investments in the rental and equipment segment both through its existing agent network and through agreements with independent service providers such as Premium.<br><br>Key financial information regarding Premium is set forth on the next page.<br><br><br>Stavanger, June 28, 2005<br><br><br>For further information, please contact:<br><br>Petter Tomren, chairman of the board of directors of IOT, phone: +47 55 22 47 10<br> <br>Premium, financial highlights follow as separate enclosure.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://www.independent.no">
http://www.independent.no</a>
<a href="/public/news/3120.doc">
Premium, financial highlights 28.06.05.doc</a>
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>IOTA - Mandatory notification of trade</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
